  ],
  "changes": [
    "Use NICE_GFX private GxEPD2 protocol HAL, without the upstream rendering/framebuffer layers.",
    "Preserve exact command bytes and SSD1675 waveform; full-screen refresh only.",
    "Normalize framebuffer coordinates to row-major controller-native portrait orientation (Adafruit source uses a transposed column buffer).",
    "Preserve SSD1619 CS edge per byte and EK79686 FLG command on each BUSY poll.",
    "Spectra6 uses continuous logical palette indices 0..5; translate to source wire codes 0,1,2,3,5,6.",
    "Split Spectra6 dual-controller data into each row left/right halves, preserving original 13.3-inch CS-specific initialization and DRF=1.",
    "Old GxEPD panels retain their own wake-up and plane polarity rather than assuming same-chip profile equivalence.",
    "All physical timing waits are delegated to the nonblocking NICE_GFX HAL."
  ],
  "constraints": [
    "No partial/differential update is advertised by these added profiles.",
    "No independent source identifies the three Spectra6 controllers: model names retained, controller reported unknown.",
    "SSD1675 waveform and literal gate bytes are retained from the pinned Adafruit source, separately from SSD1675B.",
    "Pinned Adafruit_SSD1675.cpp powerUp emits gate bytes FA 01 00 although its comment says 250-1. These literal source bytes are retained and require physical panel verification; host validation does not establish electrical or optical qualification."
  ]
